From: draft <draft@local>
Subject: [PATCH] server: --drop-reasoning-history renders assistant turns without their reasoning_content

A client that replays each assistant turn's reasoning_content (an agent
harness in a tool loop; omp does, and cannot be told not to for this
family) shows the model its own earlier thinking at every step: the
checkpoint's chat template keeps every turn's reasoning once tools are
present (drop_thinking is false then, as in the reference). Over a long
agent run the reasoning drifted into an ever flatter telegram style and
then into exact repetition; a thinking loop guard ended 16 turns in a row
and the run died with no report, also after the harness had compacted the
conversation (the flat reasoning survived the compaction).

Replaying the failed run's requests against the server (3 seeds, 2 points
of the run): with the turns' reasoning_content 3 of 6 replies looped to
max_tokens with no tool call; with the field removed 0 of 6 looped and
every reply made one sensible call.

With --drop-reasoning-history the server removes reasoning_content from
every assistant message after normalize and before the template renders
(the template then closes an empty think block, as it does for a turn
before the last user message without tools). A request without the field
is not copied. A reply's own reasoning is streamed and returned as before.
Off by default: the reference behaviour is unchanged unless the flag is
given.

